# The whole Orders flow by clicks, one screenshot per step (scripts/render-perf/README.md,
# "Orders scenes"):
#   npx tsx scripts/ui-look/look.ts --dist .ui-look/<you> --theme dark --out <dir> --steps scripts/ui-look/flows/orders-full.steps
# Selectors are the English labels of the Orders UI; when the UI is redesigned, update them here.
# Verified 2026-11-04 against the Orders UI of 5.11.0.

# Right-click an assembly, a part and a drawing: Orders > New order with these 3 files.
--scene orders-flow-start
--wait 600
--shot 01-folder
--click text=PMP-2000.sldasm
--ctrlclick text=PMP-2001.sldprt
--ctrlclick text=PMP-2003.slddrw
--rclick text=PMP-2003.slddrw
--wait 400
--hover .context-menu-item:has-text('Orders') >> nth=0
--wait 1000
--shot 02-menu
--click text=/New order with these 3 files/
--wait 2000
--shot 03-new-order

# The order is open: each model got its drawing, PDF + STEP. Add DXF to the housing and make it 8 off.
--click [aria-label='Choose the outputs of PMP-2001']
--wait 300
--shot 04-outputs-menu
--click role=menuitem[name='DXF']
--wait 800
--fill [aria-label='Quantity of PMP-2001']=8
--press Tab
--wait 800
--shot 05-edited

# Generate missing queues the jobs; the boot has no SOLIDWORKS, so record the PDFs and STEPs instead.
--click text=/Generate \d+ missing/
--wait 1200
--shot 06-generate
--eval __blueplmLookOrders.renderMissing()
--wait 1200
--shot 07-generated

# Mark sent: the DXF is still missing, so the server refuses and the dialog lists it. Send anyway.
--click button:has-text('Mark sent')
--wait 800
--shot 08-send-missing
--click button:has-text('Send anyway')
--wait 1200
--shot 09-sent

# Export zip: the fake main process downloads every output and checks its SHA-256.
--click button:has-text('Export zip')
--wait 1500
--shot 10-exported
